Verse 1:
[Eb]Lift Him up, 'tis [Ab]He that [Eb]bids you, Let the dying [Ab]look and [Eb]live;
[Eb]To all [Bb7]weary, thirsting [Eb]sinners, Living [Bb]waters [F7]will He [Bb]give;
And though [Bb7]once so meek and [Eb]lowly, Yet the [Bb7]Prince of heaven was [Eb]He;
[Eb]And the blind, who [Ab]grope in [Eb]darkness, Through the blood of [Bb7]Christ shall [Eb]see.
[Eb]Lift Him [Ab]up, the risen [Eb]Savior, High a[Bb]mid the waiting [Eb]throng;
[Eb]Lift Him [Ab]up, 'tis He that [Eb]speaketh, Now He bids you [Bb7]flee from [Eb]wrong.

Refrain:
[Eb]Lift [Ab]Him [Eb]up, [Ab]the [Eb]risen Savior,
[Eb][Bb7]High [Eb]amid [Bb]the [F7]waiting [Bb]throng;
[Bb7]Lift [Eb]Him up, [Bb7]'tis He [Eb]that speaketh,
[Eb]Now [Ab]He [Eb]bids you [Bb7]flee [Eb]from wrong.

Verse 2:
[Eb]Lift [Ab]Him [Eb]up, [Ab]this [Eb]precious Savior,
[Eb][Bb7]Let [Eb]the [Bb][F7]multitude [Bb]behold;
[Bb7]They [Eb]with willing [Bb7]hearts shall [Eb]seek Him,
[Eb]He [Ab]will [Eb]draw them [Bb7]to [Eb]His fold;
[Eb]They [Ab]shall [Eb]gather [Bb]from [Eb]the wayside,
[Eb]Hastening [Ab]on [Eb]with [Bb7]joyous [Eb]feet,
[Eb]They [Ab]shall [Eb]bear the [Ab]cross [Eb]of Jesus,
[Eb][Bb7]And [Eb]shall [Bb]find [F7]salvation [Bb]sweet.

Verse 3:
[Eb]Lift [Ab]Him [Eb]up in [Ab]all [Eb]His glory,
[Eb]'Tis [Bb7]the [Eb]Son [Bb]of [F7]God [Bb]on high;
[Bb7]Lift Him [Eb]up, His [Bb7]love shall [Eb]draw them,
[Eb]E'n [Ab]the [Eb]careless [Bb7]shall [Eb]draw nigh;
[Eb]Let [Ab]them [Eb]hear [Bb]again [Eb]the story
[Eb]Of [Ab]the [Eb]cross, the [Bb7]death [Eb]of shame;
[Eb]And [Ab]from [Eb]tongue to [Ab]tongue [Eb]repeat it;
[Eb]Mighty [Bb7]throngs [Eb]shall [Bb]bless [F7]His [Bb]name.

Verse 4:
[Eb]O [Ab]then [Eb]lift Him [Ab]up [Eb]in singing,
[Eb]Lift [Bb7]the [Eb]Savior [Bb]up [F7]in [Bb]prayer;
[Bb7]He, [Eb]the [Bb7]glorious [Eb]Redeemer,
[Eb]All [Ab]the [Eb]sins of [Bb7]men [Eb]did bear;
[Eb]Yes, [Ab]the [Eb]young shall [Bb]bow [Eb]before Him,
[Eb]And [Ab]the [Eb]old [Bb7]their [Eb]voices raise;
[Eb]All [Ab]the [Eb]deaf [Ab]shall [Eb]hear hosannah;
[Eb]And [Bb7]the [Eb]dumb [Bb]shall [F7]shout [Bb]His praise.
